  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Place the JWST NIRSpec micro-shutter array over a target-field image, search pointing and roll for the placement that catches the most catalog targets, hand-pick shutters while watching for spectra that would overlap, then save the session or export an APT-importable plan and catalog. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
